        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Slightly off topic to the thread, but Foote, do you want a place on the wiki for some of those threads?&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Idk how useful they are for the official wiki lynk. They are cool to look back and and spured some interesting discussion at the time. But they are pretty outdated as far as the information we know now. I'd question their value to newer folks digging through the wiki trying to learn actual stuff instead of being confused by my obsolete theories and ramblings</p>",
